day had broken and the World As We Knew  It fell to pieces on every corner of the  globe devastating rays of sunshine have  liquefied most of the human race the  anomalous phenomenon known as scp-001  had made the most treasured source of  light and life in the Galaxy into the  harbinger of a planetary Apocalypse in  the streets of major cities which were  once so filled with culture and activity  melting Abominations slithered along the  sidewalks and pavement a cruel parody of  the crowds and traffic that existed in  the world before the drought ravaged  Wilderness teams with countless Globs of  mutant flesh that were once proud  members of the animal kingdom even the  plants have wilted into an inert State  overwhelmed by the sun's energy to the  point of being unable to photosynthesize  it there are no planes in the sky  anymore as no pilot falling on that day  could escape the view of daylight the  boundless ocean is adrift with boats and  cruise liners occupied by an aimless  crew of amalgamations which even the  initial survivors on the lower decks and  within the rooms have long since been  assimilated into in the early months of  scp-0011 day breaks the foundation had  been able to distribute rudimentary  information on how to Shield oneself  from the perversive Rays this included a  basic but comprehensive how-to guide on  building protective clothing that would  keep out all daylight unfortunately  there is only so much benefit these  Solutions can provide as it has become  too late to save the vast majority of  humanity from their terrible melting  fate there are sadly limits on what the  foundation's foresight and knowledge  could do to prevent a worst case  scenario and many containment sites were  lost within the first 24 hours alone  this means that the veil of normalcy  that the SCP Foundation had fought so  hard to preserve has effectively cease  to exist most if not all of the  accumulated research the containment  procedures for Dangerous anomalies and  the skilled Personnel who were Brave and  foolish to think they could keep the  world safe have met with terrible Fates  in this solar scarred Hells gay if there  was ever an era where the planet and the  universe were stable and under the  control of the foundation and the o5  council that time has passed this is not  their world anymore nor is it a world  that can be ruled by any people day has  broken and this is the world of monsters  today two of these monsters in  particular find themselves on a  collision course both were once  extremely dangerous cutter class scps  contained by the foundation but through  circumstance and Ingenuity both  anomalies had freed themselves and  adapted to the harsh new reality of the  outside world they were known as  scp-076-2 Abel and  scp-682 respectively able now known in  the Fireside stories of human survivors  as the black Warrior had given himself  an armored makeover by forging his many  weapons into a day-proof second skin  straight out of Dark Fantasy media this  new edgy gothic look came complete with  a massive sword that Abel could use to  cleave straight through any fleshy freak  Show he encountered in the Wasteland he  was a true living legend now a  mysterious hero a violent demon and a  force of nature all at once in the day  he stalked through the ruins of  civilization finding whatever passed for  worthy opponents and cutting them down  at night he would seek out those  depraved Souls who would Prey Upon their  fellow human and put them to the sword  these male factors had recently become  Abel's favorite Vermin to exterminate  since they always seemed so surprised to  be on the receiving end of an ambush  being a survivor in this hellish new  world was difficult enough without the  additional strain of plotting violence  so the ones who took advantage of the  absence of laws and did so were either  exceedingly clever or simply driven out  of their wits by the desire to inflict  harm it was through several experiences  stomping out the lingering scum of the  earth that Abel discovered an unfamiliar  sense of Honor within himself it wasn't  that he grew accustomed to protecting  frail humans from Monsters but rather  the simple fact that a good fight  required two mutually adversarial  parties Bandits and serial killers could  routinely be counted on to have  delusions of grandeur accompanied by ill  intentions while their hapless victims  could not in his own Twisted way Abel  had accepted that showing Mercy to  cowards and weaklings suited his ends  after all if there were no more  Innocents Left Alive there would also be  no more reprobates to Menace them his  Quarry needed something to bait them  into emerging from the Shadows after all  despite having made the most of slim  picking there was a deep-seated part of  Abel that longed for a real challenge  the black Warrior wished to face a real  monster like himself again not the petty  brutes and former human sludge he'd been  using as substitutes 682 would be an  ideal opponent but he hadn't seen the  reptile since he was back in containment  the two had been made to fight each  other the day before all of this began  and when during the continued breach  that later ensued 682 had a makeover of  its own the highly morphic lizard had  tunneled its way out of sight 19 by  evolving barge scooping claws suited for  subterranean travel being surprisingly  intelligent for its animalistic shape  682 had managed to torture the details  of the scp-001 scenario out of an  unlucky researcher while Abel had found  a way to remain active during both day  and night  scp-682 had become a bit more selective  in its schedule this was possibly  because the creature had adapted an  internal clock by absorbing the  previously mentioned researchers  wristwatch while the sun was visible in  the sky 682 would remain dormant  underground there it could bask in the  Symphony of suffering from all the  surface dwelling living things it could  perceive with its enhanced hearing it  would lie and wait for hours  anticipating the darkness of Nightfall  once the sun had set  scp-682 would emerge and devour both  human and Abomination alike as a being  that harbored pure hatred for all things  that lived the reptile had far less  Discerning criteria for acceptable  targets than able it Unleashed its wrath  on anything that so much has gotten its  way during the nightly Feeding Frenzy  another way that 682 differed from Abel  in its post-apocalyptic way of life was  that it hadn't been given any evocative  nickname or title the reason why was  surprisingly simple 682 hadn't made its  existence known because any survivors  that encountered it never lived to tell  the tale  it was a surprise to both of them when  late one night a twist of fate brought  the monsters back together  scp-682 had just resurfaced near a small  encampment of survivors and was  approaching with the attention to  Massacre the panicking humans as the  hateful reptile Drew closer it noticed a  dark figure lurking at the other side of  the campfire it was roughly the size of  an average humanoid but instead of  running and screaming the figure stood  firm with an enormous sword in one hand  one of the fleeing humans cried out it's  the black War career we're saved this  amuse 682 and its sported a sadistic  grin as it ran toward the Survivor and  pounced while the lizard had wanted to  demonstrate how flimsy the human sense  of Salvation really was the opposite  took place the so-called black Warrior  had intercepted its jaws and was  blocking 682 with only his sword and all  the Superhuman strength he could put  behind it go now little ant the black  Warrior said following Abel's command  the human fled looking back over its  shoulder only once to gaze at the black  warrior in silent awe with that  straggler gone the two monsters were now  completely alone in the camp both  illuminated by the orange glow of  firelight they separated and began to  Circle each other memories of their old  rivalry began flooding back as both of  the now liberated Qatar classes  confirmed the identity of the other  scp-682 began to laugh as it recognized  The Stance of the ancient warrior that  had been such a Thor born in its side  back in containment isn't this Priceless  the proud and merciless able has become  a defender of those disgusting humans  scp-682 said wearing that horrible smile  once again I am not fighting for them  the black Warrior answered he lunged  forward striking a hard blow against  682's carapace the edsword bounced  upward in Recoil but not without  inflicting a deep wound that 682's  regeneration began to work overtime to  repair the reptile swiped at Abel with  its scoop claws then made further use of  them by burrowing into the ground below  Abel knew better than to follow the  creature underground and he was almost  sure that his scaly Nemesis hadn't yet  retreated he held his ground and waited  stealing himself for the moment the  creature revealed itself once more as  expected the attack came from directly  below  scp-682 breached the surface and snapped  its jaws around one of Abel's armored  legs trusting his instincts the black  Warrior struck back in the same moment  his sword stabbed into the reptile's  jaws and with a bit of strength he  leveraged his own leg free the armor was  dented but fortunately there was no  apparent holes left by 682's fangs able  had become accustomed to diligently  maintaining the condition of his armor  as even the smallest crack could in the  daylight hours cause him to lose his  solid form forever he'd made sure to do  a more thorough investigation later  after the lizard had been put in its  place the black Warrior fought  defensively minimizing the damage to his  armor while timing his strikes to keep  682 from overwhelming him with sheer  offense he could certainly go all out if  he chose to but that same part of him  that wanted a challenge w